  BPI-W2 PiKVM
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  kernel  4.9.119-BPI-W2-Kernel (BSP + HDMI RX)
  rootfs  Debian 13 (trixie) arm64

  Web UI    https://<this board's IP>/   admin / admin
  Console   root / pikvm

  ** Change both default passwords before real use **
    kvmd-htpasswd set admin
    passwd

  Handy commands:
    hdmirx-info                 detected input timings and V4L2 caps
    hdmirx-capture 30 NV16      grab 30 frames to /tmp/hdmirx.raw
    systemctl status kvmd kvmd-nginx

  USB HID (keyboard + mouse) is enabled -- connect the board's Type-C
  port to the target machine.
  MSD (virtual media) and ATX are not enabled.
